  <prompt>Change the SpaarkeAi SmartTodoWidget's default Kanban orientation from stacked rows to side-by-side columns. The enum mapping is CONFIRMED (not ambiguous, contrary to the spec's "TBD at implementation" framing): src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/widgets/SmartTodoWidget/SmartTodoWidget.tsx line ~379 sets `const [orientation, setOrientation] = React.useState&lt;Orientation&gt;('vertical')`, and the adjacent comment block (lines ~368-379) explicitly documents: "WIDGET default is 'vertical' (Today on top, Tomorrow in middle, Future on bottom — stacked rows)... The Code Page default remains 'horizontal' (columns side-by-side)." Change the widget's local default from `'vertical'` to `'horizontal'` to match the Code Page's existing side-by-side default, and update the stale comment block to reflect the new default + rationale (U-2, 2026-08-15).</prompt>

  <role>Spaarke platform developer. Expert in the shared SmartTodo Kanban widget and its CSS-only orientation-flip mechanism (NFR-03). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>SmartTodoWidget.tsx's local orientation state defaults to `'horizontal'` (side-by-side columns: left/center/right), matching the mockup intent and the Code Page's existing default; the stale "WIDGET default is 'vertical'" comment is corrected; drag-drop + selection state survive a manual orientation flip after the default change (regression, NFR-03), verified by extending the existing orientation-flip test coverage.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-09 (U-2): "the SpaarkeAi widget defaults to three side-by-side columns (left/center/right)... Verify which orientation enum value produces side-by-side and set it as the widget default." This investigation is already done — see the prompt above. The `orientation` prop threading (SmartTodoWidget → SmartTodoKanban → KanbanBoard) is a CSS-only swap per existing NFR-03 doc comments ("no React tree re-creation, so cards keep their drag-drop + selection state across an orientation flip") — this task changes only the INITIAL value, not the flip mechanism itself.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/widgets/SmartTodoWidget/SmartTodoWidget.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/components/SmartTodoKanban/SmartTodoKanban.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Phase 1 hoist gate — SmartTodoWidget.tsx lives in the shared package this task modifies; hoist must be closed first per plan.md sequencing.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT change the Code Page's orientation default (already 'horizontal'/side-by-side via useUserPreferences) — this task is widget-local only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT persist the widget's orientation via useUserPreferences — it remains intentionally widget-local per the existing documented rationale (avoids per-context Dataverse round-trips inflating cold-start time).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">NFR-03: drag-drop + selection state must survive an orientation flip with no layout glitch — regression-test this after changing the default, do not assume it still holds.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>widget-orientation-default</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-030-pane-event-bus.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-031-stage-lifecycle.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/spaarke-todo-architecture.md</file>
      <file>projects/smart-todo-r5/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/smart-todo-r5/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Read SmartTodoWidget.tsx lines ~355-395 (orientation state + surrounding comments) and SmartTodoKanban.tsx's `orientation` prop documentation to confirm the mapping before editing.</step>
    <step order="1">Change `React.useState&lt;Orientation&gt;('vertical')` to `React.useState&lt;Orientation&gt;('horizontal')` at SmartTodoWidget.tsx line ~379.</step>
    <step order="2">Rewrite the surrounding comment block (lines ~368-379) to state the NEW default and rationale: widget now defaults to side-by-side columns (matching the Code Page and the mockup intent), attributed to U-2 / smart-todo-r5 task 024, 2026-08-15. Remove or correct the now-inaccurate "WIDGET default is 'vertical'... stacked rows" language.</step>
    <step order="3">Confirm no other code path re-derives or overrides this default (e.g., a saved widget-instance config, a workspace-layout default) — grep for other `Orientation` defaults in the widget's mount path if any exist.</step>
    <step order="4">Extend/verify existing orientation-flip tests: assert the widget's INITIAL render is side-by-side (horizontal), and that flipping to vertical and back preserves drag-drop + selection state (reuse the existing NFR-03 test pattern if present; add one if not).</step>
    <step order="5">Manually verify visually: mount the widget in a narrow workspace pane and confirm 3 columns render side-by-side without overflow/clipping at typical pane widths (the prior 'vertical' default existed partly because of narrow-pane concerns per the original comment — confirm this is not a regression, or note if a responsive fallback is needed and escalate if so).</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: mark 024 ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="7">Document the confirmed enum mapping + any narrow-pane finding in projects/smart-todo-r5/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If mounting the widget at typical narrow workspace-pane widths with the new 'horizontal' (side-by-side) default causes visible column overflow/clipping that the CSS-only swap does not already handle gracefully, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than shipping a visually broken default — this may indicate the original 'vertical' default existed for a real narrow-viewport reason, not just an oversight.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Default orientation matches mockup intent">
      <steps>
        <step>Mount SmartTodoWidget fresh (no prior user interaction)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Three columns (Today/Tomorrow/Future) render side-by-side, left/center/right, not stacked</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Orientation flip preserves state (NFR-03 regression)">
      <steps>
        <step>Select a card and begin a drag operation</step>
        <step>Flip orientation via the widget's orientation toggle mid-interaction or immediately after</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Selection state and drag-drop capability survive the CSS-only flip with no layout glitch</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Render the side-by-side default in webLightTheme, then webDarkTheme</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>No visual regression; zero hex/rgb literals introduced by this change</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run vitest in the shared lib</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/widgets/SmartTodoWidget/SmartTodoWidget.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/__tests__/SmartTodoWidget.test.tsx</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a fresh SmartTodoWidget mount with no prior orientation preference, then the initial render is side-by-side columns (orientation='horizontal'), not stacked.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a side-by-side default, when the user flips to vertical and back, then drag-drop and selection state survive both flips with no layout glitch (NFR-03 regression check).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Code Page's own orientation default, then it is unchanged by this task (widget-local scope only).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass (existing + new orientation-default assertions); build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec refs: FR-09 (U-2). The "ambiguous enum naming" caveat in spec.md/CLAUDE.md Assumptions is RESOLVED by this task's own investigation — SmartTodoWidget.tsx's existing doc comment (pre-change) already states 'horizontal' = side-by-side, 'vertical' = stacked. No further enum-mapping ambiguity remains once this task's step 0 confirms it.

COMPLETION (2026-08-15): Confirmed the enum mapping directly against `KanbanBoard.tsx`'s CSS (base `board` style = `flexDirection: 'row'` = side-by-side, applied whenever NOT vertical; `boardVertical` override = `flexDirection: 'column'` = stacked, applied only when `orientation === 'vertical'`). Changed `SmartTodoWidget.tsx`'s local `useState<Orientation>` default from `'vertical'` to a new exported constant `SMART_TODO_WIDGET_DEFAULT_ORIENTATION = 'horizontal'` (single source of truth, also consumed by the new test). Rewrote the stale "WIDGET default is 'vertical'" comment block with the new default + the confirmed CSS rationale. Escalation trigger did NOT fire — `KanbanBoard`'s horizontal-mode `overflowX: 'auto'` already handles narrow-pane overflow via horizontal scroll (pre-existing 2026-06-20 round-4 fix); the prior 'vertical' default was a UX preference, not a clipping workaround. Code Page default (already 'horizontal') untouched; scoring formula untouched. Added a pure-value smoke test (`runOrientationDefaultSmokeTest`) matching the file's existing Jest-less `assert()` pattern, since `@spaarke/smart-todo-components` has no Jest config yet (build/lint = `tsc --noEmit` only; task 040 wires Jest). `npx tsc --noEmit` → exit 0. Quality gates (code-review + adr-check, FULL rigor Step 9.5): 0 Critical / 0 Warning / 0 Suggestion; ADR-021 + ADR-012 compliant. Only the 2 concurrency-scoped files were touched; nothing committed. Full writeup: `projects/smart-todo-r5/notes/task-024-widget-columns.md`.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
